THE HEADLINE FINDING, AND IT IS THE SAME IN EVERY ARM:
  ***  NOT ONE VIOLATION ON ANY AIRPORT IS EVER PRICED AT THE 5 % CAP.  ***
  v3 within_shape airside by cap: CYXY none at all; SPJC 62 @1.0 % + 11
  @1.5 %; HECA 2221 @1.0 % + 147 @1.5 %.  The interior law mints nothing in
  v2 and nothing in v3.  What the interior cap changes is how much the
  interior may MOVE, and every metre it moves is absorbed by the STRICT
  class bounding it.  Widening the interior class therefore worsens the
  strict class monotonically at HECA:

    interior class        HECA within_shape airside    HECA airside
    v1  removed entirely            770                    1167
    v2  non-ring-adjacent          1383                    1599
    v3  + non-corridor ring edges  2368                    2560

  A2's own prediction held — the ~648 ring edges it targeted DO stop being
  violations, because they now pass at 5 % — but the surface they no longer
  hold tilts, and the movement surfaces take it.  A2 is the right reading
  of 2026-08-21b (a non-frontage ring edge IS a generic pair) and the wrong
  lever for the bar.

  HECA v3 residual, classified: 2205 apron within_shape airside rows = 786
  FRONTAGE CHORDS + 1419 GENERIC, and since none carry the 5 % cap every
  generic one is a CORRIDOR-CROSSING ring edge (1366 priced unified:apron,
  25 apron:spine, 28 foreign).  Severity followed the count: >2x-cap 447
  (battery) -> 663 (v2) -> 1117 (v3); accumulated excess 4332 -> 4564 ->
  6905 percentage-points.  Head sites (30.11814,31.41057),
  (30.11818,31.41055), (30.11843,31.41048) at 1.37-1.41 % against 1.00 %.

  SPJC v3 residual (+24), as the lead asked it be split: 62 apron rows =
  15 FRONTAGE CHORDS (chord p50 54.9 m, max 177.9 m) + 47 GENERIC, all
  strict, so all CORRIDOR-CROSSING ring edges (35 unified:apron, 11
  apron:spine, 1 foreign); plus 11 junction rows @1.5 %.  TWO POPULATIONS,
  and they need different fixes:
    * the METRE-heavy rows are hairline in grade — 1.019-1.097 % against
      1.000 % on 55-178 m chords, way -10113, sites (-12.019228,-77.110061),
      (-12.019231,-77.110059), (-12.029663,-77.104875);
    * the SEVERE rows are a localised WELD CLUSTER on sub-metre chords —
      39 of the 53 >2x rows are <= 5 m long, 10 more <= 20 m, |de| only
      0.16-0.45 m, all around (-12.021394,-77.110990) where ways -10113 /
      -10162 / -10698 / -10699 meet.  That is a seat/weld defect, not a
      grading one.
  NO FIX ATTEMPTED (A2 is a correction of the lead's clause, and the
  instruction on an over-bar airport is STOP + attribution).

WHAT THE COMPOSED LANE DID BUY, and it holds across v2 and v3:
TRANSVERSE IS SOLVED.  Airside transverse is at or below the battery on
